<section id="A1.SSx1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Toolset Details</h3>

<div id="A1.SSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To effectively address complex verification tasks that require multi-modal misinformation detection, we design an extensible toolset for T<sup id="A1.SSx1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>Agent. We provide a detailed description of each tool in the toolset in this section.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SSx1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SSx1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Web Searching</span>
This toolset is used to gather reliable knowledge from the web for information verification. We integrate the Google Search API <span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">2</span>
              
              
            https://developers.google.com/custom-search/v1/overview</span></span></span> and Wikipedia API <span id="footnote3" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">3</span>
              
              
            https://www.wikipedia.org/</span></span></span>, which are particularly effective in retrieving general web content and encyclopedic knowledge, respectively.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SSx1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SSx1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Time Detection</span>
This module is responsible for identifying the earliest appearance time of an image. To achieve this, we utilize TinEye <span id="footnote4" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">4</span>
              
              
            https://tineye.com/</span></span></span>, a reverse image search engine, to trace the earliest online publication date of a given visual content.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SSx1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SSx1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Forgery Detection</span>
This toolset includes pre-trained forgery detection models designed to detect digital manipulations. The system supports the integration of new forgery detection models to meet the user’s needs. For the AMG <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guo et al. 2025</a>)</cite> benchmark, we employ PSCC-NET(Liu et al. 2022), a powerful manipulation detection network, to identify subtle image tampering.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SSx1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SSx1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Counterfactual Detection</span>
Unlike forgery detection, which focuses on identifying whether media has been digitally altered or synthesized (e.g., deepfakes), this module detects inconsistencies between the depicted scene and real-world facts, i.e., counterfactual content. We use LLava-34B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al. 2024a</a>)</cite>, a powerful vision-language model, to analyze images for logically or physically implausible elements.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SSx1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SSx1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Image Understanding</span>
This component provides a detailed, question-driven interpretation of visual content. In our implementation, the image understanding model is aligned with the backbone model of the overall framework.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SSx1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SSx1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Entity Recognition</span>
This tool enables precise identification of key entities within visual content, such as people, landmarks, and organizations. We use the Baidu Entity Recognition API <span id="footnote5" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">5</span>
              
              
            https://ai.baidu.com/tech/imagerecognition/general</span></span></span>, which specializes in extracting entities from images.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SSx2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">T<sup id="A1.SSx2.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>Agent  Pseudocode</h3>

<div id="A1.SSx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our method T<sup id="A1.SSx2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>Agent  consists of a Multi-source Verification MCTS and a Tool Selection mechanism.
Alg. <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ T2Agent Pseudocode ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ T2Agent: A Tool-augmented Multimodal Misinformation Detection Agent with Monte Carlo Tree Search" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> presents the pseudocode of Multi-source Verification MCTS. Our method begins by initializing a root node representing the task of verifying news authenticity, with child nodes corresponding to various forgery sources weighted by an LVLM analysis.
During each iteration, promising nodes are selected using a modified UCT criterion to balance exploration and exploitation effectively.
Upon selecting a specific node, the agent initiates a simulation process. During this simulation, the agent iteratively performs reasoning steps (thoughts), executes actions, and collects observations. This iterative reasoning continues until either a conclusive answer is found or the predefined maximum search depth
<math id="A1.SSx2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> is reached.
At the termination of the simulation, an evaluation phase assesses the entire simulation process using a dual scoring mechanism that integrates both reasoning trajectory scores and confidence scores. The results from this evaluation are then backpropagated to update the values of the relevant nodes.
Finally, the decision-making component aggregates the verification results from the updated nodes to produce a final determination on the authenticity of the news.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Multi-source Verification MCTS </figcaption>
<div id="alg1.3" class="ltx_listing ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_middle ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing" style="width:455.3pt;">
<div id="algx1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              
            Initial state <math id="algx1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, LVLM model <math id="algx1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{LVLM}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{LVLM}</annotation></semantics></math>, number of generated actions <math id="algx1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, depth limit <math id="algx1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, number of simulations <math id="algx1.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, exploration weight <math id="algx1.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>, hyperparameter <math id="algx1.l1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              
            Initialize the tree with sub-task nodes. <span id="algx1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="algx1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Initialization
</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              
            <span id="algx1.l3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="algx1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leftarrow 1,\dots,K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leftarrow 1,\dots,K</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx1.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span> <span id="algx1.l3.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="algx1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Simulation Loop
</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              <math id="algx1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> root node

</div>
<div id="algx1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              Select node<math id="algx1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\leftarrow\arg\max_{s^{\prime}\in children(s)}\left[V(s^{\prime})+C\sqrt{\frac{\ln(N(s)+1)}{N(s^{\prime})+1}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\leftarrow\arg\max_{s^{\prime}\in children(s)}\left[V(s^{\prime})+C\sqrt{\frac{\ln(N(s)+1)}{N(s^{\prime})+1}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algx1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="algx1.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Selection
</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              <span id="algx1.l6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span> <math id="algx1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> not terminal and depth <math id="algx1.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;d</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx1.l6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span> <span id="algx1.l6.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="algx1.l6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Expansion and simulation
</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              
               <span id="algx1.l7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="algx1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> has unvisited children <span id="algx1.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              
                 Expand <math id="algx1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> by generating <math id="algx1.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> new child nodes using <math id="algx1.l8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{LVLM}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{LVLM}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              
               <span id="algx1.l9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="algx1.l9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              
               Select next node <math id="algx1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\prime}\in children(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\prime}\in children(s)</annotation></semantics></math> using modified UCT:

</div>
<div id="algx1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              <span id="algx1.l11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="algx1.l11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              Combine scores: <math id="algx1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(s)=\alpha S_{t}^{T}+(1-\alpha)S_{t}^{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(s)=\alpha S_{t}^{T}+(1-\alpha)S_{t}^{C}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx1.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="algx1.l12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Evaluation
</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              <span id="algx1.l13.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="algx1.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leftarrow T-1,\dots,0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leftarrow T-1,\dots,0</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx1.l13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span> <span id="algx1.l13.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="algx1.l13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Backpropagation
</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              
               <math id="algx1.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(s_{t})\leftarrow\frac{V(s_{t})(N(s_{t}))+V(s)}{N(s_{t})+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(s_{t})\leftarrow\frac{V(s_{t})(N(s_{t}))+V(s)}{N(s_{t})+1}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              <span id="algx1.l15.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="algx1.l15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
              
            <span id="algx1.l16.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="algx1.l16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
              
            <span id="algx1.l17.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> Early stop with an answer <span id="algx1.l17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span> <span id="algx1.l17.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="algx1.l17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Decision making
</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              return answer

</div>
<div id="algx1.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
              
            <span id="algx1.l19.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              <math id="algx1.l20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(real)=\prod_{i=1}^{n}{\left(1-p\left(\text{fake}^{i}\right)\right)}^{\left(1/n\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mtext>fake</mtext><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(real)=\prod_{i=1}^{n}{\left(1-p\left(\text{fake}^{i}\right)\right)}^{\left(1/n\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              <math id="algx1.l21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="answer=arg\max\left(p(real),\left\{p(fake^{i})\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">answer=arg\max\left(p(real),\left\{p(fake^{i})\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l22" class="ltx_listingline">
              
            <span id="algx1.l22.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="algx1.l22.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SSx2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SSx2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Although the full set of tools offers broad functionality, not all tools are equally valuable for every task <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lu et al. 2025</a>)</cite>. To balance efficiency and performance, we leverage greedy search to systematically identify the most effective subset of tools. Alg. <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ T2Agent Pseudocode ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ T2Agent: A Tool-augmented Multimodal Misinformation Detection Agent with Monte Carlo Tree Search" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> presents the pseudocode of the tool selection mechanism. In practice, we select a subset (100 samples) of all data samples for evaluation function <math id="A1.SSx2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> to save time.
It is worth to notice that our method is differnet from OctoTools <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lu et al. 2025</a>)</cite>.
OctoTools evaluates each tool independently by adding it to a fixed base toolset and measuring its individual contribution. In contrast, our method incrementally adds tools one by one in a greedy fashion, evaluating the combined effect at each step.
We conduct experiments to compare our method with OctoTools <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lu et al. 2025</a>)</cite>. Our approach employs Web Searching, Counterfactual Detection, and Entity Recognition, while Octo-Tools additionally incorporates Image Understanding. Experimental results show that our method achieves an F1 score of 0.568, outperforming Octo-Tools (F1 = 0.550). This suggests that although Image Understanding can be beneficial when used in isolation, its integration into a multi-tool framework may lead to performance degradation. One possible explanation is that Image Understanding can partially substitute for other tools—such as Entity Recognition—but with lower accuracy. This redundancy and reduced precision may interfere with the verification process, ultimately harming performance.
The results shows that our strategy enables a more accurate assessment of tool selection.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> Tool selection </figcaption>
<div id="alg2.3" class="ltx_listing ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_middle ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing" style="width:455.3pt;">
<div id="algx2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              
            <span id="algx2.l1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> Toolbox <math id="algx2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}=\{d_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}=\{d_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, base toolset <math id="algx2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\text{base}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\text{base}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              
            <span id="algx2.l2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> Optimized toolset <math id="algx2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              
            <math id="algx2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Acc}_{\text{baseline}}\leftarrow\text{Acc}(\mathcal{D}_{\text{base}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>Acc</mtext><mtext>baseline</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>Acc</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Acc}_{\text{baseline}}\leftarrow\text{Acc}(\mathcal{D}_{\text{base}})</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx2.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="algx2.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Stage 1: Baseline setup
</span>
</div>
<div id="algx2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              
            <span id="algx2.l4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each <math id="algx2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="algx2.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx2.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">such that</span> <math id="algx2.l4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}\notin\mathcal{D}_{\text{base}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}\notin\mathcal{D}_{\text{base}}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx2.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span> <span id="algx2.l4.4" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="algx2.l4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Stage 2: Individual tool evaluation
</span>
</div>
<div id="algx2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              <math id="algx2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{i}\leftarrow\mathcal{D}_{\text{base}}\cup\{d_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{i}\leftarrow\mathcal{D}_{\text{base}}\cup\{d_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              <math id="algx2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Acc}_{i}\leftarrow\text{Acc}(\mathcal{D}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>Acc</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>Acc</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Acc}_{i}\leftarrow\text{Acc}(\mathcal{D}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              <math id="algx2.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{d_{i}}\leftarrow\text{Acc}_{i}-\text{Acc}_{\text{baseline}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>Acc</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mtext>Acc</mtext><mtext>baseline</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{d_{i}}\leftarrow\text{Acc}_{i}-\text{Acc}_{\text{baseline}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              <span id="algx2.l8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="algx2.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{d_{i}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{d_{i}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx2.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="algx2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              
               <math id="algx2.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\text{base}}\leftarrow\mathcal{D}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\text{base}}\leftarrow\mathcal{D}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx2.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              <span id="algx2.l10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="algx2.l10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="algx2.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              
            <span id="algx2.l11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="algx2.l11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="algx2.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              
            <math id="algx2.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}^{*}\leftarrow\mathcal{D}_{\text{base}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}^{*}\leftarrow\mathcal{D}_{\text{base}}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx2.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="algx2.l12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Stage 3: Select optimized toolset
</span>
</div>
<div id="algx2.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              
            <span id="algx2.l13.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Return</span> <math id="algx2.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SSx3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Experiment Details</h3>

<div id="A1.SSx3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SSx3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In our implementation, we set the number of sampled nodes to <math id="A1.SSx3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=2</annotation></semantics></math> and the exploration weight to <math id="A1.SSx3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=2</annotation></semantics></math>. Additionally, the hyperparameter <math id="A1.SSx3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.5</annotation></semantics></math> is used to balance the reasoning trajectory score and the result confidence score in the evaluation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SSx4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">More Results</h3>

<div id="A1.SSx4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SSx4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We present the results on the AMG benchmark in Table <a href="#A1.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ More Results ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ T2Agent: A Tool-augmented Multimodal Misinformation Detection Agent with Monte Carlo Tree Search" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>. It is important to note that the AMG dataset is initially designed for supervised learning. All compared methods, including CAFE (Chen et al. 2022), MCAN (Wu et al. 2021), and MGCA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guo et al. 2025</a>)</cite>, are trained or fine-tuned on the provided training set. In contrast, our proposed T<sup id="A1.SSx4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>Agent  is based on tool-augmented tree search with large language models, requiring no training or fine-tuning.
Specifically, T<sup id="A1.SSx4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>Agent  with GPT-4o obtains an F1 score of 0.510, surpassing CAFE (Chen et al. 2022) and MCAN (Wu et al. 2021). Notably, the test set of AMG has a highly imbalanced class distribution. Under such conditions, the F1 score is a particularly meaningful metric, and our method’s competitive performance on the F1 score suggests its power without any task-specific training.
Despite underperforming compared to MGCA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guo et al. 2025</a>)</cite>, which achieves the highest F1 score of 0.567, our method demonstrates superiority in the following aspects: (1) Rapid adaptation and low-cost deployment:
Although training-based methods can achieve strong performance, they (Chen et al. 2022; Wu et al. 2021; Guo et al. 2025) typically require designing different model architectures for different scenarios and often suffer from poor out-of-domain generalization. In contrast, our T<sup id="A1.SSx4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>Agent  is training-free and can handle emerging misinformation without any additional training, making it particularly valuable in the early stages of information outbreaks.
(2) Data privacy and regulatory compliance:
In domains with strict privacy and compliance requirements—such as healthcare or finance—fine-tuning on task-specific training data may be infeasible or even prohibited. Our method circumvents this issue by avoiding task-specific training altogether.
(3) Benefit from powerful LLMs:
As shown in the results, as the model size increases (from GPT-4.1-nano to GPT-4o), the performance of T<sup id="A1.SSx4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>Agent  consistently improves, rising from 0.503 to 0.579. This indicates that the performance may be further improved with a more powerful model.</p>
</div>
